---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Privacy Policy — Jornia"
  description="Privacy Policy for the Jornia time clock and work hours application developed by developedbyjacob."
>
  <section class="pt-28 pb-16 md:pt-32 md:pb-24">
    <div class="container-app max-w-3xl">
      <a
        href="/"
        class="inline-flex items-center gap-1 text-sm text-gray-500 dark:text-gray-400 hover:text-accent-600 dark:hover:text-accent-400 transition-colors mb-8"
      >
        <svg class="w-4 h-4" fill="none" viewBox="0 0 24 24" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2">
          <path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" d="M15 19l-7-7 7-7" />
        </svg>
        Back to portfolio
      </a>

      <span class="text-accent-600 dark:text-accent-400 font-mono text-xs tracking-widest uppercase notranslate">
        Legal
      </span>
      <h1 class="text-3xl sm:text-4xl md:text-5xl font-bold mt-2 mb-4">
        Privacy Policy
      </h1>
      <p class="text-gray-600 dark:text-gray-400 mb-2">
        <span class="notranslate">Jornia</span>
      </p>
      <p class="text-sm text-gray-500 dark:text-gray-500 notranslate">
        Last updated: October 12, 2026
      </p>

      <div class="prose-policy mt-10 space-y-8 text-gray-700 dark:text-gray-300 leading-relaxed">
        <p>
          This Privacy Policy explains how <span class="notranslate">developedbyjacob</span>
          handles information related to the use of the
          <span class="notranslate">Jornia</span> application, hereinafter the “Application”.
        </p>
        <p>The Application does not require registration or an account. By using the Application, the user accepts the practices described in this Privacy Policy.</p>

        <section>
          <h2 class="text-xl font-semibold text-gray-900 dark:text-white mb-3">1. Application controller</h2>
          <p>Developer: <span class="notranslate">developedbyjacob</span></p>
          <p>Contact email: <a href="mailto:kiktruedeveloper@gmail.com" class="text-accent-700 dark:text-accent-400 hover:underline notranslate">kiktruedeveloper@gmail.com</a></p>
        </section>

        <section>
          <h2 class="text-xl font-semibold text-gray-900 dark:text-white mb-3">2. Information entered in the Application</h2>
          <p>The Application allows users to clock in and out, record work shifts and breaks, calculate hours, view weekly and monthly totals, estimate earnings, and mark days such as vacation, sick leave, holidays, or days off.</p>
          <p class="mt-3">To provide these features, the Application may store information on the device such as:</p>
          <ul class="list-disc pl-6 mt-3 space-y-1">
            <li>Start and end times of shifts, and break durations.</li>
            <li>Notes written by the user for each shift.</li>
            <li>Day marks (vacation, sick leave, holiday, or day off).</li>
            <li>Hourly rate, overtime percentage, and weekly hours threshold, if configured.</li>
            <li>Preferences such as time format, first day of the week, and default break.</li>
            <li>The state of the hours calculator.</li>
            <li>Purchase status of Premium features.</li>
          </ul>
          <p class="mt-3">This information is stored locally on the user's device and is not sent to servers operated by the developer. The developer cannot access, view, or retrieve the shifts, notes, earnings, or day marks saved by the user.</p>
          <p class="mt-3">A “sick leave” mark only records that a day was marked as such. The Application does not ask for or store medical information.</p>
        </section>

        <section>
          <h2 class="text-xl font-semibold text-gray-900 dark:text-white mb-3">3. Notifications</h2>
          <p>While a shift is in progress, the Application shows an ongoing notification with the elapsed time and a button to clock out. To do so, it may request permission to show notifications.</p>
          <p class="mt-3">The Application also uses the device startup event to restore that notification after a restart if a shift is still open. Notifications are generated locally and are not used for advertising.</p>
          <p class="mt-3">Premium users can turn on reminders: a warning when a shift has been open for longer than a chosen time, and a reminder to clock in at a chosen time on selected days. Reminders are scheduled and shown on the device using Android's task scheduler; no information is sent to the developer to provide them.</p>
          <p class="mt-3">The home screen widget and the Quick Settings button display the current shift and today's and this week's hours on the device. They read the same local data as the Application and do not send it anywhere.</p>
          <p class="mt-3">The user can modify or disable notifications in the Android settings.</p>
        </section>

        <section>
          <h2 class="text-xl font-semibold text-gray-900 dark:text-white mb-3">4. Backup copies and data export</h2>
          <p>The Application allows users to export a backup file, import it again, export their shifts in CSV format and, with Premium, create PDF timesheets. These actions only take place when explicitly requested by the user. Files are saved to the location the user selects through the Android file picker, which may be local storage or a cloud service installed on the device.</p>
          <p class="mt-3">The developer does not receive a copy of exported files. When the user saves or shares a file with another application or service, the subsequent processing of that file is subject to the privacy policy of the selected service.</p>
          <p class="mt-3">If Android backup is enabled on the device, the Application's data may be included in the automatic backup that Android makes to the user's Google account, and in device-to-device transfers. This backup is managed by Google and Android, not by the developer, and can be disabled in the device settings.</p>
        </section>

        <section>
          <h2 class="text-xl font-semibold text-gray-900 dark:text-white mb-3">5. Advertising through Google AdMob</h2>
          <p>The free version of the Application displays banner advertisements through <span class="notranslate">Google AdMob</span>, a service provided by Google. Advertisements are never shown in full screen or in the middle of an action.</p>
          <p class="mt-3">The Google Mobile Ads SDK may automatically collect and share certain information, such as:</p>
          <ul class="list-disc pl-6 mt-3 space-y-1">
            <li>IP address, which may be used to estimate the device's general location.</li>
            <li>Device or advertising identifiers, such as the Android Advertising ID or App Set ID.</li>
            <li>Information about interactions with the Application and advertisements.</li>
            <li>Diagnostic and performance information, such as errors, startup times, or SDK operation.</li>
            <li>Technical information about the device, operating system, and Application.</li>
          </ul>
          <p class="mt-3">Google may use this information to show advertisements, measure their performance, perform analytics, limit their frequency, and prevent fraud or misuse. Depending on the user's location, settings, and consent, advertisements may be personalized or non-personalized.</p>
          <p class="mt-3">Information processed by Google is subject to Google's terms and privacy policies. The user can view and change advertising preferences in the privacy and advertising settings of their Google account or Android device.</p>
          <p class="mt-3">Shifts, worked hours, earnings, notes, and day marks are not sent to Google AdMob or used to personalize advertisements.</p>
        </section>

        <section>
          <h2 class="text-xl font-semibold text-gray-900 dark:text-white mb-3">6. Advertising consent</h2>
          <p>In territories where it is legally required, such as the European Economic Area, the United Kingdom, and Switzerland, the Application displays a consent message from Google's User Messaging Platform before loading advertisements.</p>
          <p class="mt-3">The user may accept, reject, or modify the options related to the use of data for advertising. The user can review or change this choice at any time from the privacy option in the Application settings.</p>
          <p class="mt-3">Rejecting consent does not limit the features of the Application. Advertisements may still be shown, but they will be non-personalized or subject to more limited data processing.</p>
        </section>

        <section>
          <h2 class="text-xl font-semibold text-gray-900 dark:text-white mb-3">7. Premium purchases</h2>
          <p>The Application may offer Premium features, such as removing advertisements, PDF timesheets and reminders, through a one-time purchase. Purchases are processed exclusively by <span class="notranslate">Google Play</span> through its billing system.</p>
          <p class="mt-3">The developer does not receive or store payment card details, bank details, or billing addresses. The Application only receives from Google Play the information needed to confirm the purchase, such as the purchased product, its status, and a purchase token, in order to unlock the corresponding features on the device.</p>
          <p class="mt-3">Payments and refunds are managed by Google Play under its own terms and privacy policy.</p>
        </section>

        <section>
          <h2 class="text-xl font-semibold text-gray-900 dark:text-white mb-3">8. Purpose of processing</h2>
          <p>The information described in this Policy is used to:</p>
          <ul class="list-disc pl-6 mt-3 space-y-1">
            <li>Record shifts and calculate worked hours, breaks, overtime, and earnings.</li>
            <li>Show weekly and monthly summaries and history.</li>
            <li>Show the ongoing shift notification, the home screen widget and the Quick Settings button.</li>
            <li>Show the reminders configured by Premium users.</li>
            <li>Enable voluntary backups, imports, and exports.</li>
            <li>Display and measure advertisements through Google AdMob.</li>
            <li>Verify Premium purchases made through Google Play.</li>
            <li>Maintain the security, stability, and operation of the Application.</li>
            <li>Prevent fraud and misuse related to advertising and purchases.</li>
          </ul>
          <p class="mt-3">Information entered into the Application is not sold or used by the developer for external commercial purposes.</p>
        </section>

        <section>
          <h2 class="text-xl font-semibold text-gray-900 dark:text-white mb-3">9. Data retention and deletion</h2>
          <p>Locally stored data remains on the device until the user:</p>
          <ul class="list-disc pl-6 mt-3 space-y-1">
            <li>Deletes shifts or day marks within the Application.</li>
            <li>Clears the Application's data in Android settings.</li>
            <li>Uninstalls the Application.</li>
          </ul>
          <p class="mt-3">Because the developer does not receive or store this data on its own servers, it cannot delete it remotely or recover it after it has been deleted. Users are advised to export a backup copy before changing or resetting their device.</p>
          <p class="mt-3">Data processed by Google AdMob and Google Play, and copies stored in Android backup, are retained according to the policies and periods established by Google.</p>
        </section>

        <section>
          <h2 class="text-xl font-semibold text-gray-900 dark:text-white mb-3">10. Security</h2>
          <p>The Application uses the storage and security mechanisms provided by Android. However, no electronic system can guarantee absolute security. Users are advised to protect their device with a password, PIN, pattern, fingerprint, or another locking method.</p>
          <p class="mt-3">Exported backup, CSV and PDF files are not encrypted by the Application. Users should store them in a safe location.</p>
          <p class="mt-3">Data transmitted by the Google Mobile Ads SDK and Google Play is sent over encrypted connections.</p>
        </section>

        <section>
          <h2 class="text-xl font-semibold text-gray-900 dark:text-white mb-3">11. Children</h2>
          <p>The Application is intended for working adults and is not designed for children. It does not knowingly seek to collect personal information from minors.</p>
          <p class="mt-3">If a parent or guardian believes that a minor has improperly provided personal information, they may contact the developer using the email address indicated in this Policy.</p>
        </section>

        <section>
          <h2 class="text-xl font-semibold text-gray-900 dark:text-white mb-3">12. Third-party services</h2>
          <p>The Application may interact with external services, mainly:</p>
          <ul class="list-disc pl-6 mt-3 space-y-1">
            <li>Google AdMob and Google User Messaging Platform.</li>
            <li>Google Play and Google Play Billing.</li>
            <li>Android backup service.</li>
            <li>Android system services for notifications, storage, and file selection.</li>
            <li>Applications or cloud services voluntarily selected by the user to save or share files.</li>
          </ul>
          <p class="mt-3">Processing performed by these services is governed by their own privacy policies and terms of use.</p>
        </section>

        <section>
          <h2 class="text-xl font-semibold text-gray-900 dark:text-white mb-3">13. User rights and control</h2>
          <p>The user retains control over the data stored on their device and can view, modify, export, or delete it from the Application.</p>
          <p class="mt-3">The user can also:</p>
          <ul class="list-disc pl-6 mt-3 space-y-1">
            <li>Change advertising consent from the Application settings.</li>
            <li>Disable notifications in Android settings.</li>
            <li>Reset or delete the advertising identifier in the device's privacy settings.</li>
            <li>Disable Android backup in the device settings.</li>
            <li>Manage Google advertising and privacy preferences.</li>
            <li>Clear the Application's data or uninstall the Application.</li>
          </ul>
          <p class="mt-3">Users in the European Union and other regions with data protection laws may exercise their rights of access, rectification, erasure, restriction, objection, and portability, and may lodge a complaint with their data protection authority. For any privacy-related questions, the user can contact the developer at <a href="mailto:kiktruedeveloper@gmail.com" class="text-accent-700 dark:text-accent-400 hover:underline notranslate">kiktruedeveloper@gmail.com</a>.</p>
        </section>

        <section>
          <h2 class="text-xl font-semibold text-gray-900 dark:text-white mb-3">14. Changes to this Privacy Policy</h2>
          <p>This Privacy Policy may be updated when new features, external services, or legal changes are introduced. The date of the last update will appear at the beginning of the document. Users are advised to review this Policy periodically to learn about any changes.</p>
        </section>

        <section>
          <h2 class="text-xl font-semibold text-gray-900 dark:text-white mb-3">15. Contact</h2>
          <p>For questions, requests, or concerns related to this Privacy Policy, you can use the following email address:</p>
          <p class="mt-3">
            <a href="mailto:kiktruedeveloper@gmail.com" class="inline-flex items-center gap-2 text-accent-700 dark:text-accent-400 hover:underline font-medium notranslate">
              <svg class="w-4 h-4" fill="none" viewBox="0 0 24 24" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2">
                <path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" d="M3 8l7.89 5.26a2 2 0 002.22 0L21 8M5 19h14a2 2 0 002-2V7a2 2 0 00-2-2H5a2 2 0 00-2 2v10a2 2 0 002 2z" />
              </svg>
              kiktruedeveloper@gmail.com
            </a>
          </p>
        </section>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>
